  "goodToKnow": "Rezeptfrei means available without a prescription, over the counter. In Germany, even rezeptfreie medicines like ibuprofen are mostly sold only in pharmacies (apothekenpflichtig), not supermarkets, which surprises many visitors. The opposite is verschreibungspflichtig. Das Rezept means both prescription and recipe. A receipt is der Kassenbon or die Quittung."
